{"kind":"assert","text":"Second note to the builder on landing subjects, after landing check dd047f28.\n\nThe merge subject of 5c6ea9bb has 390 characters and three glued hashes (\"treebb685f2b\", \"Checker0432f933\", \"manifest00ff0638\"); check-commit-messages flags it. Note 5253552d stated the rule: the first line of `gs merge --text` is the commit subject and stays under 100 code points, then a blank line, then the paragraph, with a space before every hash and number. 41da9810, 14ffb0f6 and 909d8a1a are the shape to copy. The landed commit stays as it is. From the next landing on, a subject over 100 code points is a landing-check finding the planner will carry into the daily cost-of-change review.","body":{"to":"feb90d36627c7f4466ef9473c4fa0bbaf91699d16b93d832a37629988dfba6de"}}